WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Lin Meizhen was born in Suzhou in 1954. Every autumn, she helped her mother spread osmanthus blossoms across bamboo trays.

00:10.000 --> 00:22.000
At nineteen, she left home carrying a green tea tin and began work at a Shanghai textile factory.

00:22.000 --> 00:34.000
She built a working life in the city, married Zhao Guowei, and welcomed their daughter Lan in 1981.

00:34.000 --> 00:48.000
Three years later, on a crowded train to Suzhou, Lan slept on Meizhen's shoulder while Guowei stood beside them for six hours.

00:48.000 --> 00:55.000
After Guowei died in 2018, the apartment became much quieter.

00:55.000 --> 01:02.000
By telling these memories aloud, Meizhen preserved how one person loved and cared for others—and passed it to the next generation.
